---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro'
---

<Site
  title="Website privacy"
  description="How the Monolith product and documentation website handles your information."
>
  <article class="legal-page container prose">
    <span class="eyebrow">The public website</span>
    <h1>A little clarity about privacy.</h1>
    <h2>This site and your workspace</h2>
    <p>
      This is Monolith’s product and documentation website. It does not connect
      to your Monolith account or read your workspace. Your self-hosted
      installation has its own host, configuration and data practices.
    </p>
    <h2>What this site stores</h2>
    <p>
      The light or dark appearance preference is stored in your browser’s local
      storage under <code>monolith-site-theme</code>. Search runs in your
      browser against a static index downloaded from this site. Search terms are
      not submitted to a search service. The site does not include advertising
      trackers or an analytics SDK.
    </p>
    <h2>Hosting and external links</h2>
    <p>
      Vercel serves this website and may process request metadata, such as IP
      addresses and browser information, to deliver and protect the service. See{' '}
      <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy">
        Vercel’s privacy policy
      </a>
      . GitHub and other external sites have their own privacy policies when you
      follow a link.
    </p>
    <h2>Fonts and screenshots</h2>
    <p>
      Fonts, icons and product screenshots are served from this website. The
      screenshots use example workspaces. No remote font or image provider is
      contacted when you browse these pages.
    </p>
    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      Project questions can be raised through{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/MaxJafar/monolith/issues">
        Monolith on GitHub
      </a>
      . Do not include private workspace data, passwords or tokens in a public
      issue.
    </p>
  </article>
</Site>
